course: dictionary
lesson: 15883
title: Hard to make out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from small parts you already know. Unintelligibility is one of them. Break it into pieces: un- means not, intelligible means able to be understood, and -ity turns the idea into a noun, a state or quality. So unintelligibility is the state of not being able to be understood.
explain: «The radio was so full of crackle that the news had complete unintelligibility.» The crackle is the clue. The words were there, but nobody could make them out. In everyday talk you would just say «you can't make it out».
explain: The word is often used about speech, handwriting and signals. «The doctor's handwriting had such unintelligibility that the chemist sent the prescription back.» Read the words around it and ask: what would fit here? Something like "being impossible to read" fits, so that is the meaning.
fact: Unintelligibility is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «a lot of unintelligibility», not «two unintelligibilities».
fact: Intelligible means able to be understood, so unintelligible means not able to be understood.
fact: The word parts are un- (not), intelligible (can be understood) and -ity (a state or quality).
fact: «Unintelligibility» means the state of being impossible or very hard to understand, especially speech or writing.
fact: It is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in books, reports and science talk. In everyday talk, say «you can't make it out».
exercise: «The static on the line caused such unintelligibility that we hung up.» What does unintelligibility mean here? | Being very loud | Being very neat | *Being impossible to make out | Being very quick
exercise: Which word is the noun for the state of not being understood? | *Unintelligibility | Understanding | Intelligence | Intelligent
exercise: Mum says, «I can't make out your scribble, it's pure unintelligibility!» What is she saying about the scribble? | It is very long | It is neat and easy to read | *It is almost impossible to read | It is very colourful
test: «Two friends from different countries tried to chat, but the unintelligibility between them made them laugh.» What does unintelligibility mean? | Being a long holiday | Being very easy to follow | *Being very hard to understand | Being hungry for food
test: Which meaning fits unintelligibility best? | It means being tall for your age | It means being kind to others | *It means being impossible or very hard to understand | It means being quick at sums
exam: Which sentence uses unintelligibility correctly? | The unintelligibility of the cake was delicious | *The unintelligibility of the mumbled speech meant nobody could follow it | The unintelligibility of the sunny day was lovely | The unintelligibility of the speech made every word clear
